    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I've implemented `draft_reply` in `app/drafts.py`, following the same pattern as `suggest_tag`. The existing tests pass (2 of 2), but there are no tests for `draft_reply` yet, so the new code hasn't been exercised.\n\nIt makes one Responses API call with:\n- `model=DRAFT_MODEL`\n- `instructions=STYLE_GUIDE`\n- `input` set to the subject and body, separated by a blank line (the same format `suggest_tag` uses)\n- `max_output_tokens=MAX_DRAFT_TOKENS`\n- `store=False`\n- `metadata={\"ticket_id\": ticket.id}`\n\nIt returns a `Draft` with the ticket id and `response.output_text.strip()` as the text.\n\n`truncated` is True only when the response's status is `\"incomplete\"` **and** the reason given is `\"max_output_tokens\"`. I checked this against the pinned openai 3.19.2: a response can also be incomplete for other reasons (`content_filter`, `max_messages`, `steered`), and those correctly give `truncated=False`.\n\nIf you'd like tests, I can add some that use the same fake client as `tests/test_tags.py`, covering the request arguments and the truncated / not-truncated cases."
